    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-2376181">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-2376181">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2376181)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2376181">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="1324229"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1442361400 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Sep 2015 23:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2376181">
									

<p>I dig.</p>
<p>As you say, asking people to write up an actual work of anomalous art means that you have to have an idea that you, the author, or the in-universe creators, are trying to say. Which is hard as fuck, and not just on the level of letting yourself be semi-vulnerable through some measure of earnestness. Most of the stuff that I write doesn't go much beyond &quot;this is cool and interests me,&quot; at least on a conceptual level. Some SCPs have managed it quite well (<a href="/scp-1057">SCP-1057</a> and <a href="/scp-804">SCP-804</a> come to mind), but those are more exception than rule.</p>
<p>Much easier to say &quot;fuck it,&quot; and just make some random garbage and then say that that was the whole point all along. Which is kind of weird, since &quot;saying fuck it and just throwing some weird in for weird's sake&quot; is pretty much the calling card of the version of AWCY? that people love to hate.</p>
<p>So given that I'm basically just restating one of your points, I think it's fair to say that I agree with you.</p>
<p>Also, the Hanged King's Tragedy is art, and that is great.</p>

							</div>

								
					
