					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=388108&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605818406" alt="Djoric" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=388108)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;" >Djoric</a></span> <span class="odate time_1442363675 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Sep 2015 00:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2376208">
									

<p>I wrote an in-universe <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/a-study-of-anomalous-art">thing</a> on this subject a while ago, and I am very much in favor of more varied anomalous art.</p>
<p>I am also very much a fan of AWCY being a bunch of violent, talentless hacks that either murdered or scared off any of the talent they once had, and are stuck gibbering to themselves in an echo chamber of inane shitposting. &quot;If they were any good or had anything meaningful to say, they wouldn't be AWCY&quot;, I say, and I will stick with it.</p>
<p>I really want to see non-AWCY artists, though. My first essay was an attempt to get that ball rolling, though it didn't go very far.</p>
<p>I'm considering another in-universe essay, detailing specific anartist groups. This essay might be the motivation I need to get it done.</p>

							</div>

								
