					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=388108&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605818406" alt="Djoric" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=388108)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;" >Djoric</a></span> <span class="odate time_1442405689 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Sep 2015 12:14</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2376459">
									

<p>Again, I see this as just a continuation of the status quo.</p>
<p>I honestly feel that people need to be broken out of thinking that AWCY is the be-all end-all of anart. Subsequently, I give great encouragement to not using AWCY at all.</p>
<p>Because even if the end result is thought-provoking, it will still turn into &quot;oh look, it's AWCY again&quot;</p>
<p>I myself am getting tired of the repetitive blandness of formulaic Wondertainment articles, so I dunno why you're aiming for that. I'm tired of samey AWCY articles too.</p>
<p>The answer I came up with to break away from samey Wondertainment articles is &quot;non-toy articles that don't bear the name but are connected via mythos cues&quot;, (though that has not actually been implemented, damnable format). You'll get a similar answer from me about AWCY - scrap the name, scrap the MO, <em>do something different</em>.</p>
<p>I hope that clears things up, because it feels like we are having some major miscommunication here.</p>

							</div>

								
