					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/steeltitan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1871133); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1871133&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605818406" alt="Steeltitan" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1871133)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/steeltitan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1871133); return false;" >Steeltitan</a></span> <span class="odate time_1442377302 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Sep 2015 04:21</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2376334">
									

<p>Oh! Thank you! I had forgotten about those pieces. They also seem to kind of be anart in a way. One is living anart by the artist, and one is a musical anart piece by a guy who probably had anart stuff but didn't realize it. So in the end there are small anarts that aren't AWCY. One represents the currents of time, and the other the hopeful, determined human belief in true love.</p>

							</div>

								
					
